WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.368
The school compares enteral, parenteral and intraosseous routes. Use those categories to understand delivery, not as a ladder in which every sick patient automatically moves to IV or IO.
学校比较经肠道、非肠道及骨内途径。分类用于理解送入，不是所有病重者自动升级静脉或骨内的梯子。

00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:26.064
The route must fit the indication, formulation, patient and actual authority. IV access has risks and may not be needed when an effective less-invasive treatment is available.
途径须适应证、剂型、患者及真实权限都符合。静脉有风险，有有效低侵入治疗时可能不需。

00:00:26.064 --> 00:00:41.832
The school table lists IV or IO as preferred in anaphylaxis. That is not the initial-care rule: current E zero nine prioritizes intramuscular epinephrine. Do not delay indicated IM treatment while seeking a line.
学校表把全身过敏列为首选静脉或骨内，这不是初始照护规则。当前E09优先肌注肾上腺素，不能为找通路延误有适应证肌注。

00:00:41.832 --> 00:00:51.864
Generic poor-perfusion concerns do not cancel that indication-specific rule. State the treatment and route together, then check its current clinical pathway.
笼统灌注差顾虑不能取消该特定适应证规则。应将治疗及途径一起说，再核当前临床路径。

00:00:51.864 --> 00:01:03.600
The intima is the inner endothelial lining; valves are folds of that inner layer. Mechanical or chemical irritation can contribute to inflammation and thrombosis.
内膜是内侧内皮衬里，瓣膜是该层折叠。机械或化学刺激可促炎症和血栓。

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:15.456
The media includes smooth muscle and elastic tissue and is thinner than the comparable arterial layer. Sympathetic tone can alter venous calibre, particularly in cold or shock.
中膜含平滑肌及弹性组织，较相应动脉层薄。交感张力可改变静脉口径，冷或休克尤其明显。

00:01:15.456 --> 00:01:24.384
The externa provides connective support. These are tissue layers, not three separate lumens into which a needle may be placed interchangeably.
外膜提供结缔支持。这些是组织层，不是针可以随便放的三个管腔。

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:38.496
Veins generally return blood toward the heart at lower pressure and hold substantial blood volume. Direction defines a vein; oxygen content is not the universal definition, because pulmonary veins are an important exception.
静脉通常以较低压力向心回流并容纳较多血量。定义是流向，不是氧含量；肺静脉是重要例外。

00:01:38.496 --> 00:01:49.728
Flow depends on catheter and tubing properties as well as the driving pressure. A narrower or longer catheter generally offers more resistance under comparable conditions.
流量依导管及管路性质，也依驱动压力。可比条件下，较窄或较长导管通常阻力更大。

00:01:49.728 --> 00:02:00.768
For gravity delivery, bag height relative to the site contributes pressure. A kink, closed clamp, retained constricting band or bent joint can restrict flow.
重力给入时，药袋相对穿刺部位高度贡献压力。打折、夹闭、未松止血带或关节弯曲可限流。

00:02:00.768 --> 00:02:11.280
A running drip chamber is not proof that the fluid is entering the vein. Check the site and delivered volume, especially after movement or a sudden rate change.
滴斗在滴不证明液体进入静脉。搬动或速度突变后尤其要看部位及已入量。

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:24.528
Choose access and equipment for the actual need rather than automatically choosing the largest catheter or a universal proximal site. Avoid unnecessary attempts and do not delay appropriate transport.
按真实需要选通路器械，不自动选最大导管或一律近端。避免无谓尝试，也不能延误适当转运。

00:02:24.528 --> 00:02:36.504
Shock or cold can reduce tissue perfusion and delay IM or SC absorption. The finding should change reassessment and the clinical plan, not justify an improvised second route.
休克或冷可降低组织灌注、延迟肌肉皮下吸收。这应改变复评及计划，不授权临时自创第二途径。

00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:51.144
IV dosing bypasses absorption, but reaching the target and producing effect still depend on circulation and pharmacodynamics. Direct access does not make onset literally instantaneous for every medicine.
静脉绕过吸收，但到靶点及产生作用仍依循环和药效学。直接通路不让每种药都字面瞬时起效。

00:02:51.144 --> 00:03:04.584
IO is not a blanket solution for every collapsed vein, child or conscious shocked patient. The current PCP conditions and age restrictions apply even if a general physiology diagram looks favourable.
骨内不是所有塌陷静脉、儿童或清醒休克患者的通用解决。一般生理图看起来有利，也仍适用当前PCP条件和年龄限制。

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:17.256
If a route is failing, support immediate breathing or circulatory threats, identify why and request appropriate help. The correct alternative must be clinically suitable and authorized.
途径失效时先支持即时呼吸循环威胁、找原因并请求适当支援。正确替代须既临床适合又获授权。

00:03:17.256 --> 00:03:29.112
A swallowed medicine passes through the gastrointestinal system. A suitable sublingual medicine is absorbed through mucosa; it does not need to travel through the gut to produce that intended effect.
吞下药经胃肠系统；适合舌下药经黏膜吸收，不需先走胃肠才产生该预期效应。

00:03:29.112 --> 00:03:38.688
The school groups PO and SL as enteral for teaching, but do not infer identical absorption, first-pass handling or clinical suitability.
学校把口服和舌下合为经肠道教学，但不能推断吸收、首过或适合度完全相同。

00:03:38.688 --> 00:03:52.560
Assess whether the patient can cooperate, manage secretions and protect the airway, and whether active vomiting or distress prevents safe use. Do not provoke gagging as a shortcut to certifying swallowing safety.
评估患者能否合作、处理分泌物及保护气道，活动呕吐或痛苦是否妨碍安全使用。不能刺激咽反射来捷径证明吞咽安全。

00:03:52.560 --> 00:04:06.312
If the prescribed route is unsafe, hold and use the appropriate authorized pathway. Crushing an unsuitable tablet, changing its route or giving a liquid to an unprotected airway is not a safe workaround.
规定途径不安全时暂停并用适当获授权路径。碾不适合片剂、换途径或往无保护气道口给液体，都不是安全变通。

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:20.304
A subcutaneous dose is deposited in tissue beneath the dermis and above muscle. An intramuscular dose is deposited within the selected muscle. The intended layer affects absorption and technique.
皮下药放在真皮下、肌肉上组织；肌注放在选定肌肉内。目标层次影响吸收和技术。

00:04:20.304 --> 00:04:33.960
Needle length, gauge, site, tissue thickness, medication and volume must be selected together. A needle too short may miss muscle; a poorly placed deep needle can injure underlying structures.
针长、粗细、部位、组织厚、药和体积须一起选。过短可能没到肌肉，深针定位差可伤下方结构。

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:46.056
The diagram is a layer concept, not a body landmark map. Learn the actual landmarks on a model with the instructor and verify the specific device or medication procedure.
图只是层次概念，不是身体定位图。要与教员在模型学真实标志并核具体装置或药物规程。

00:04:46.056 --> 00:04:56.328
Do not use the textbook's largest listed IM volume as the permitted volume for every site or child. Site capacity and formulation requirements differ.
不能用教材最大肌注体积作为每个部位或儿童允许体积。部位容纳和剂型要求不同。

00:04:56.328 --> 00:05:09.120
Confirm the specific indication and IM formulation before preparation. IM is a preferred emergency route in some conditions, not merely a backup whenever an IV was inconvenient.
配制前核具体适应证及肌注剂型。某些情况肌注就是急救首选，不只是静脉不方便时的备用。

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:23.616
Verify the dose, volume and appropriate equipment, and label the prepared medication. Choose the site specified by the indication and current procedure; anaphylaxis epinephrine uses the anterolateral mid-thigh.
核剂量、体积及适当器械，标配好药。按适应证和当前流程选部位；全身过敏肾上腺素用大腿前外侧中段。

00:05:23.616 --> 00:05:35.760
Inspect skin and identify the actual landmarks rather than choosing an arbitrary distance from the shoulder. Position the patient so the intended muscle is accessible and relaxed.
看皮肤并识别真实解剖标志，不能随便量离肩多远。让患者体位使目标肌可接近且放松。

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:49.584
Use hand hygiene, the indicated PPE, aseptic handling and an accessible sharps container. The first live injection must be within the school's supervised authorization process, not self-practice from this slide.
使用手卫生、适当PPE、无菌操作及可及锐器盒。首次真实注射必须在学校督导授权流程内，不能只照幻灯自行练。

00:05:49.584 --> 00:05:59.856
After the complete medication check, clean the intended site with the approved preparation and let it dry. Avoid touching and contaminating the prepared area.
完整药物核查后，用批准制剂清洁目标处并待干，避免触碰污染已准备区域。

00:05:59.856 --> 00:06:13.536
Using the instructed landmark and patient-specific equipment, stabilize the tissue and enter the muscle with the taught technique, generally at ninety degrees. Needle depth cannot be determined from the angle alone.
用教过标志和针对患者器械，固定组织并按所教技术入肌，通常90度。不能只由角度决定深度。

00:06:13.536 --> 00:06:28.992
Follow the current medication and device procedure for aspiration and delivery rate. The older textbook's routine aspiration rule is not universal for all injections, and a vaccine rule is not automatically a rule for every therapeutic drug.
回抽及速度按当前药物装置规程。旧教材常规回抽不是所有注射通用规则，疫苗规则也不自动适用所有治疗药。

00:06:28.992 --> 00:06:43.176
Withdraw safely, activate the safety device and immediately dispose without recapping. Provide the indicated site care and document dose, site, time and response, including any unexpected reaction.
安全退针、启安全装置并立即丢锐器，不回套。按需护理部位并记剂量、部位、时间及反应，包括意外反应。

00:06:43.176 --> 00:06:55.824
Verify that the medicine, volume and SC route are appropriate. Choose an intact taught site and the device and needle that reach the subcutaneous layer without unintentionally reaching muscle.
核药、体积和皮下途径合适，选完整所教部位，选能到皮下且不误入肌肉的装置针。

00:06:55.824 --> 00:07:09.624
SC angle depends on tissue and device, commonly forty-five to ninety degrees in general teaching. The older Nancy passage uses forty-five degrees throughout; that is not every current product's instruction.
皮下角度依组织装置，一般教学常为45至90度。旧Nancy段统一45度，不是每种当前制剂说明。

00:07:09.624 --> 00:07:22.968
Do not universally aspirate or massage after a SC dose. The candidate Canadian procedure says not to massage; actual aspiration and site care must follow the medicine and current procedure.
不能一律皮下回抽或注后按摩。加拿大候选规程说不按摩；真实回抽及部位护理应遵具体药和当前流程。

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:34.488
Dispose safely and monitor the site and patient. Poor perfusion may delay absorption, and repeated doses need the actual route-specific interval and cumulative check.
安全处置并监测部位患者。灌注差可能延迟吸收，重复剂要查真实途径间隔和累计量。

00:07:34.488 --> 00:07:46.176
Intranasal delivery requires an appropriate medication and device. A syringe with a mucosal atomizer and a sealed unit-dose spray have different preparation and delivery instructions.
鼻内给药需适当药和装置。注射器黏膜雾化头与密封单剂鼻喷，有不同配制给药说明。

00:07:46.176 --> 00:07:59.112
For the syringe procedure, verify concentration and calculated volume before attaching the atomizer. Remove the fill tip safely and inspect for nasal blood or mucus that could obstruct delivery.
注射器流程中，接雾化头前核浓度和计算体积。安全移除抽药头，检查鼻腔血液黏液是否堵塞。

00:07:59.112 --> 00:08:12.864
Current PR eleven accounts for the atomizer's zero-point-one-millilitre dead space and prepares half-dose delivery to each nostril. Follow that exact device procedure, not a remembered instruction from a different spray.
当前PR11考虑雾化头0.1毫升死腔，并分别准备半剂给两侧鼻孔。按该装置真实流程，不套另一喷雾记忆。

00:08:12.864 --> 00:08:25.896
Coordinate access to the nose without unnecessarily interrupting life-sustaining ventilation. Naloxone delivery is part of an airway-first plan, not a reason to leave the patient unventilated.
协调接近鼻部，避免不必要中断维持生命通气。纳洛酮是气道优先计划一部分，不是让患者无通气的理由。

00:08:25.896 --> 00:08:37.680
The current syringe-atomizer procedure limits volume to one millilitre per nostril. A correct drug amount may be unsuitable intranasally if its concentration requires too much volume.
当前注射器雾化流程限每鼻孔1毫升。药量算对，但浓度要求体积过大时，可能不适合鼻内。

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:50.160
For a fictional one-point-six-milligram dose at one milligram per millilitre, the intended drug volume is one point six millilitres, or zero point eight per nostril before device preparation.
虚构1.6毫克、每毫升1毫克，目标药液体积1.6毫升，装置准备前每鼻孔0.8毫升。

00:08:50.160 --> 00:09:03.816
At half a milligram per millilitre, the same amount would need three point two millilitres, or one point six per nostril, beyond that limit. Do not solve it by flooding the nose or inventing repeat intervals.
若每毫升0.5毫克，同量需3.2毫升，每鼻孔1.6，超过限制。不能灌鼻或自创重复间隔解决。

00:09:03.816 --> 00:09:17.304
Resolve the concentration or an authorized alternative with the current pathway. Reassess actual delivery and clinical response; an atomized dose is not proof that an exact systemic amount has been absorbed.
按当前路径解决浓度或获授权替代，复查真实给入及临床反应。雾化剂量不证明精确等量已体循环吸收。

00:09:17.304 --> 00:09:30.912
Verify the inhaler name, strength, remaining doses, expiry and prior use. Prepare and shake or prime only as required by that product, and inspect the spacer and valves.
核吸入器名、强度、余量、效期及前剂。按制剂要求准备、摇或预喷，检查储雾罐和瓣。

00:09:30.912 --> 00:09:44.544
Use an effective mouthpiece or mask seal. Deliver one actuation at a time into the spacer and coach the appropriate slow inhalation or approved tidal-breathing technique for that patient and device.
用有效口嘴或面罩密合，每次向储雾罐一喷，指导适合该患者装置的慢吸或获准潮气呼吸技术。

00:09:44.544 --> 00:09:56.208
An able patient may hold the breath as comfortably instructed, but do not require a distressed patient to perform an impossible ten-second hold or stop needed oxygen unnecessarily.
能配合者可按舒适指导屏气，但不能要求呼吸窘迫者完成不可能10秒屏气，也不能无谓停必需氧。

00:09:56.208 --> 00:10:07.200
Repeat only within the indicated regimen and reassess. A correctly counted number of sprays does not establish delivery if the seal failed or the patient could not inhale.
只在规定方案内重复并复评。若密合失败或不能吸入，喷数正确不证明已有效送入。

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:20.832
Verify the intended drug and concentration and use the required diluent and device. Flow requirements and fill volume depend on the nebulizer; the textbook's single six-litre setting is not universal.
核目标药浓度，用所需稀释液及装置。驱动流和装液量依雾化器，教材单一6升设置非通用。

00:10:20.832 --> 00:10:33.312
Keep the chamber and interface in the intended orientation and coach breathing that the patient can manage. A visible mist outside the mask is not proof that the intended amount reaches the airways.
保持药杯界面正确方向，指导患者做得到的呼吸。面罩外有雾不证明预期药量到气道。

00:10:33.312 --> 00:10:49.128
Use the current infection-control and device precautions. For ineffective breathing, ventilation support takes priority; a trained compatible in-line system may be part of the plan, but must not compromise BVM effectiveness.
按当前感染及装置防护。呼吸无效时通气支持优先；受训相容管内系统可作为计划，却不能损BVM有效性。

00:10:49.128 --> 00:11:04.320
Reassess airflow, work, speech and the adverse response. Increasing fatigue, decreased awareness or poor air movement requires urgent escalation, not more time waiting beside a running nebulizer.
复查气流、呼吸功、说话和不良反应。疲劳增加、意识降或气流差需紧急升级，不能继续守着雾化器等。

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:18.216
A line should have an actual indicated use. A vague expectation that the hospital may want an IV later is not enough by itself, and an effective less-invasive route may make a line unnecessary.
通路须有真实适应用途。笼统想医院以后可能要静脉，本身不足；有效低侵入途径可能使其不必。

00:11:18.216 --> 00:11:28.944
Verify access authority as well as drug authority. Current BCEHS PCP under-twelve cannulation restrictions apply even when a school model demonstrates the procedure.
药权限外也核通路权限。即使学校模型展示操作，当前BCEHS PCP未满12穿刺限制仍适用。

00:11:28.944 --> 00:11:41.688
Trace the established line to the patient and inspect the site, solution, connectors and any other running treatment. Do not assume patency from a label or a historic successful insertion.
追既有管至患者，查部位、液体、接头及其他运行治疗。不能凭标签或过去穿刺成功假定通畅。

00:11:41.688 --> 00:11:54.048
This week prepares IV-push medication checks; the following school weekend develops access skills. Passing a preparation lesson does not demonstrate actual cannulation competence.
本周准备静推核查，后续学校周末发展通路技能。通过准备课不代表已会真实穿刺。

00:11:54.048 --> 00:12:04.488
IV push means a syringe dose through appropriate vascular access. Some drugs require slow delivery, so the word push does not establish speed.
静推是用注射器经适当血管通路给一剂。有些药需慢给，“推”字不确定速度。

00:12:04.488 --> 00:12:18.000
Complete the medication and patient checks, including current dilution, compatibility and administration time. Clean the connector using the actual device and antiseptic procedure and let it dry as required.
完成药及患者核查，包括当前稀释、相容及时间。按实际接头和消毒流程清洁并按需待干。

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:31.584
Confirm line identity and patency using the approved method. Pain, swelling, leakage or resistance requires reassessment; do not force the dose to make a difficult line work.
用批准方法核身份及通畅。疼痛、肿、漏或阻力需重评，不能用力推药让难用管“通”。

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:46.176
Deliver at the drug-specific rate while observing the patient and site. Device-specific clamping or connection technique must prevent backflow and unintended delivery, not blindly reproduce an older needle-port diagram.
按药物特定速度，观察患者和部位。具体夹管连接应防倒流及非预期给入，不能盲照旧针刺接口图。

00:12:46.176 --> 00:12:57.744
After syringe delivery, part of a dose may remain in the connector or extension. The actual line dead space and compatible flush procedure matter to what reaches the patient.
注射器给后，部分药可留接头或延长管。真实死腔及相容冲管流程决定到患者什么。

00:12:57.744 --> 00:13:10.200
Use the appropriate compatible flush volume and method for the device, patient and medicine. The older textbook's twenty-millilitre flush is not a universal rule for every age and access.
按装置、患者和药用适当相容冲管量及方法。旧教材20毫升不是所有年龄通路通用规则。

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:21.456
A rapid flush can rapidly deliver a slow-push drug still in dead space. The medication-specific rate must be preserved where relevant, including the residual dose.
快冲可把死腔中原应慢推药迅速送入。相关时须保持药物特定速度，包括残留药。

00:13:21.456 --> 00:13:33.312
Do not automatically run the line wide open to clear it. Restore the intended ongoing rate and document actual drug and relevant fluid delivery, then reassess effect and harm.
不能一律开到最大来清管。恢复预期持续速度，记实际药及相关液体送入，复评益处伤害。

00:13:33.312 --> 00:13:46.632
Fluid or medication outside the intended vessel may cause local injury. Hyperosmolar products such as dextrose can be particularly damaging; an IV label does not prevent tissue exposure.
液体或药在目标血管外可造成局部损伤。葡萄糖等高渗制剂尤其可能伤组织；贴静脉标签也防不了外渗。

00:13:46.632 --> 00:13:59.928
Watch for new pain, swelling, coolness, leakage, resistance or altered flow, and compare the site with the patient's report. Not every complication presents with every sign.
观察新痛、肿、凉、漏、阻力及流量变，结合患者报告。并非每并发症都有全部征象。

00:13:59.928 --> 00:14:12.456
Stop the implicated administration and follow the specific extravasation procedure, preserving the device if the protocol needs it for aspiration or treatment. Seek appropriate clinical guidance.
停相关给药，按具体外渗流程；若流程需经原装置回吸或处理，要按规定保留，寻适当临床指导。

00:14:12.456 --> 00:14:25.968
Do not force a flush through the suspect site or improvise heat, cold, massage or an antidote. Subsequent access and treatment depend on the actual drug, tissue and authorized plan.
不能对疑似部位强冲，也不自创热敷、冷敷、按摩或解药。后续通路治疗依真实药、组织及获授权计划。

00:14:25.968 --> 00:14:37.200
The vascular marrow network connects with systemic venous circulation, allowing indicated IO delivery when peripheral access cannot be established in the permitted clinical setting.
骨髓血管网与体静脉循环相连，可在允许临床环境、外周无法建立时进行有适应证骨内给入。

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:48.960
The bony space resists collapse, but that does not guarantee correct placement, flow or immediate peak drug effect. Placement and ongoing tissue checks are still essential.
骨性空间抗塌陷，却不保证放置、流量或药物立即峰效都正确。仍必须核放置和持续组织情况。

00:14:48.960 --> 00:15:02.280
Complications include painful infusion, extravasation, compartment injury, infection and device movement. A conscious patient's pain plan requires the appropriately authorized practitioner.
并发包括输注痛、外渗、筋膜室伤、感染及装置移位。清醒患者止痛计划需相应获授权医护。

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:14.232
For PCP, review the exact current PR twelve pathway from the pharmacology lecture. Do not choose IO solely because a generic school case describes severe dehydration.
PCP应重查药理课所述当前PR12准确路径。不能只因学校泛例写严重脱水就选骨内。

00:15:14.232 --> 00:15:26.016
One school subsection lists proximal humerus as a recommended PCP IO site. The checked current BCEHS procedure explicitly restricts PCP placement to a tibial site.
学校某分节将肱骨近端列PCP推荐骨内部位；已核当前BCEHS流程明确PCP仅胫骨。

00:15:26.016 --> 00:15:39.456
The same source supplies generic needle lengths and a ten-to-twenty-millilitre saline-plus-lidocaine instruction. Do not treat those as a patient-specific device selection or an unrestricted local-anesthetic order.
同源给通用针长及10至20毫升盐水加利多卡因说法，不能当针对患者选针或无限局麻医嘱。

00:15:39.456 --> 00:15:53.856
Use current patient, site, authority and manufacturer criteria. Confirm placement and protect the site using the actual taught procedure; a single reassuring sign is not a guarantee against extravasation.
按当前患者、部位、权限及制造标准。用真实所教流程确认并保护部位；单一放心征象不保证无外渗。

00:15:53.856 --> 00:16:09.072
The saved subsection also contains unrelated template prose. It is not a clinical instruction or a learning objective. The course uses substantive clinical content and identifies corrections instead of filling slides with that text.
存档该节还含无关模板文字，不是临床指令或学习目标。本课采用实质临床内容并标修正，不用它凑幻灯。

00:16:09.072 --> 00:16:18.624
After moving the patient, immediately check the person before the equipment. An airway or perfusion problem is more urgent than a neat-looking dressing.
搬动后先立即查人，再查设备。气道或灌注问题比敷料好看更紧急。

00:16:18.624 --> 00:16:31.368
Then trace the treatment: interface seal, connectors, tubing, clamp, line site and securement. A device can move while the pump display or drip chamber still appears unchanged.
再追治疗：界面密合、接头、管、夹、穿刺处及固定。设备可能已移动，但泵显示或滴斗看起来不变。

00:16:31.368 --> 00:16:40.920
Reconfirm actual rate and delivered amount, especially with gravity systems. Inspect for a pulled catheter or hidden swelling under a blanket.
尤其重力系统要再核真实速度和给入量，查是否导管拉出或毛毯下藏肿。

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:51.288
Document a changed route, stopped treatment or failed delivery truthfully. Do not assume that the prepared amount equals the administered amount after a disconnection.
如实记换途径、停治疗或给入失败。断开后不能假定配好量等于给入量。

00:16:51.288 --> 00:17:04.944
An adult is vomiting and cannot reliably respond. A family member hands you an oral prescription and asks for the usual dose. There is no demonstrated patient request and oral safety is not established.
成人呕吐且不能可靠回应，家属递口服处方要给常用剂量。没有证实患者请求，也没建立口服安全。

00:17:04.944 --> 00:17:14.328
Begin immediate assessment and support the airway and breathing as needed. Do not administer the oral product merely because its label and dose are familiar.
先即时评估，按需支持气道呼吸。不能因标签剂量熟就给口服。

00:17:14.328 --> 00:17:26.952
Determine the underlying emergency and applicable authority. A separate indicated emergency treatment may exist, but you may not invent an injectable conversion of the family's oral medicine.
确定潜在急症及适用权限。可能另有有适应证紧急治疗，但不能自创把家属口服药改注射。

00:17:26.952 --> 00:17:40.176
Explain why the route is unsafe, seek the appropriate support and document the findings and plan. The safe decision integrates physiology, consent, route and scope rather than using any one alone.
解释途径为何不安全，寻适当支援并记录发现计划。安全决策整合生理、同意、途径及权限，不单凭其一。

00:17:40.176 --> 00:17:51.288
At the school station, verbalize the specific route decision before handling equipment. Identify the indication, authority and a reason that this route could fail.
学校站点拿器械前先口述具体途径决策，识别适应证、权限及一个可能失效原因。

00:17:51.288 --> 00:18:02.160
Demonstrate preparation on the assigned training equipment, then have the instructor check landmarks, needle choice, interface or connection and medication-specific details.
在指定训练器械示范准备，再请教员核定位、针选择、界面连接及药物特定细节。

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:15.528
Perform the current taught delivery sequence and immediately reassess the intended effect and relevant harms. If a problem is introduced, stop the implicated action and explain your recovery plan.
执行当前所教给药顺序，立即复评预期作用及相关伤害。若设置故障，停相关行动并解释恢复计划。

00:18:15.528 --> 00:18:27.384
Use the bilingual reading checklist to rehearse, but obtain the actual school skill sign-off. A completed video or worksheet does not demonstrate safe psychomotor performance by itself.
用双语阅读清单演练，但要拿真实学校技能签核。看完视频或填完表本身不能证明安全动作能力。
